n the last stored range started at or beyond the query end, prematurely stopping reverse iteration even when earlier ranges overlapped. The fix loops past non-overlapping trailing ranges until it finds an overlap or exhausts the iterator. The upstream property test added by this commit compares forward results with reversed backward results.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:28:30.963666+00:00"}
{"commit": "b3a59e6641a9e3869791f781abbae98f828f91c9", "id": "b3a59e6641a9e3869791f781abbae98f828f91c9-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Reversal changes are not part of the upstream fix", "repo": "https://github.com/jeffparsons/rangemap", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T005709Z-3b179786", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/b3a59e6641a9e3869791f781abbae98f828f91c9-1/20260924T005709Z-3b179786/origin.json": "2a7f3db46c5446187e2734a1466187bc08fb82ba885911264a209e441bf361f4", "evidence/b3a59e6641a9e3869791f781abbae98f828f91c9-1/20260924T005709Z-3b179786/proposal.json": "4ae9c93b4256938e97718cf38fbe3eac3b1aa05e8bd47dd34d12a99bc5f73a6f"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "rangemap", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix `PartialEq` implementation for `RangeMap`", "summary": "`RangeMap::PartialEq` delegated to `self.btm == other.btm`. The inner `BTreeMap` keys are `RangeStartWrapper`, which orders and compares only on `range.start`, so maps with matching starts but different ends (e.g. `{1..3 => 0}` vs `{1..4 => 0}`) compared equal. The fix switches to `self.iter().eq(other.iter())`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:57:09.328061+00:00"}
